that has come out called Istio.

00:38:22.740 --> 00:38:27.460
Istio is what we call a
service mesh tool, which

00:38:27.460 --> 00:38:30.400
helps you manage your
microservices within something

00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:33.010
like the Kubernetes
infrastructure.

00:38:33.010 --> 00:38:37.270
Now, Apigee itself has
a integration with Istio

00:38:37.270 --> 00:38:39.640
where, as you can
imagine, you have

00:38:39.640 --> 00:38:42.820
tons of these microservices
within your Kubernetes

00:38:42.820 --> 00:38:43.870
infrastructure.

00:38:43.870 --> 00:38:46.000
But you also want to
be able to then manage

00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:48.880
some of these services as APIs.

00:38:48.880 --> 00:38:52.690
So as part of the Istio
expansion capabilities,

00:38:52.690 --> 00:38:56.230
we have built an adaptor
between Istio and Apigee

00:38:56.230 --> 00:38:59.470
where you can take some
of those microservices

00:38:59.470 --> 00:39:02.380
and actually manage them
through the management

00:39:02.380 --> 00:39:05.710
platform within Apigee itself.

00:39:05.710 --> 00:39:09.700
For more details, just do a--

00:39:09.700 --> 00:39:12.130
go to our Apigee
Documentation site.

00:39:12.130 --> 00:39:15.560
And there is an Istio section
specific to that as well.

00:39:15.560 --> 00:39:17.740
How to monetize products?

00:39:17.740 --> 00:39:21.490
So Apigee is a complete
API management platform,

00:39:21.490 --> 00:39:25.190
and as part of that, we do
have a monetization module.

00:39:25.190 --> 00:39:28.780
So you can actually create what
we call different rate plans

00:39:28.780 --> 00:39:31.270
against different API products.

00:39:31.270 --> 00:39:32.890
These products can
then be something

00:39:32.890 --> 00:39:36.010
that you make publicly
available or you push

00:39:36.010 --> 00:39:38.900
towards specific consumers.

00:39:38.900 --> 00:39:42.490
They can be defined
as simple as a bucket

00:39:42.490 --> 00:39:46.130
where a consumer would need
to pay a monthly charge.

00:39:46.130 --> 00:39:50.590
Or you can come up with
more exotic sort of plans

00:39:50.590 --> 00:39:54.970
where perhaps it's tiered,
where the first tier

00:39:54.970 --> 00:39:56.440
they would pay x amount.

00:39:56.440 --> 00:40:00.220
And then once they exceeded
an amount of calls,

00:40:00.220 --> 00:40:02.480
they would then be
charged less or more,

00:40:02.480 --> 00:40:04.910
depending on what type of
model that you're trying to do.

00:40:04.910 --> 00:40:08.380
The question, is this specific
to just retail organizations

00:40:08.380 --> 00:40:11.830
or is this something you are
seeing across all industries

00:40:11.830 --> 00:40:12.640
and verticals?

00:40:12.640 --> 00:40:15.580
That is a great question,
and it is across all

00:40:15.580 --> 00:40:17.950
industries and verticals.

00:40:17.950 --> 00:40:21.260
Retail is something that
we see a lot happening.

00:40:21.260 --> 00:40:24.070
But naturally, across
financial and health services

00:40:24.070 --> 00:40:26.230
as well, they are
getting more and more

00:40:26.230 --> 00:40:28.043
comfortable with cloud.

00:40:28.043 --> 00:40:29.710
And therefore, they're
actually starting

00:40:29.710 --> 00:40:32.830
to leverage Apigee
as the platform

00:40:32.830 --> 00:40:36.460
to help them move and
modernize into the cloud.

