00:41:17.680 --> 00:41:21.520
How does this help in
traffic management?

00:41:21.520 --> 00:41:25.060
So Apigee, as a complete
API management platform,

00:41:25.060 --> 00:41:27.850
has a number of policies
that actually help you

00:41:27.850 --> 00:41:29.140
with traffic management.

00:41:29.140 --> 00:41:31.960
So things like
quota are available

00:41:31.960 --> 00:41:36.070
and also where you can
actually define things

00:41:36.070 --> 00:41:40.870
like x number of calls per
month, per day, per minute.

00:41:40.870 --> 00:41:43.270
It's up to you what
you want to define.

00:41:43.270 --> 00:41:45.940
We also do have things like
SpikeArrest, which helps

00:41:45.940 --> 00:41:47.500
you smooth out your traffic.

00:41:47.500 --> 00:41:50.530
So think of it as
a way to prevent

00:41:50.530 --> 00:41:55.810
DDoS calls into your platform.

00:41:55.810 --> 00:41:59.120
We also have things that can
actually improve performance.

00:41:59.120 --> 00:42:01.600
So things like caching
are available as part

00:42:01.600 --> 00:42:04.990
of the policies to
actually allow you

00:42:04.990 --> 00:42:07.000
to define what your keys are.

00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:11.230
And then if a request comes
in with the same request,

00:42:11.230 --> 00:42:17.690
same key, Apigee itself can
serve the traffic out into--

00:42:17.690 --> 00:42:20.080
back into the API
consumer itself,

00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:22.120
thereby avoiding having
to go all the way

00:42:22.120 --> 00:42:26.170
back up to the back-end
system to retrieve.

00:42:26.170 --> 00:42:29.090
Do you normally need a
service mesh like Istio

00:42:29.090 --> 00:42:32.420
if your microservices
are on PCF?

00:42:32.420 --> 00:42:33.200
No.

00:42:33.200 --> 00:42:37.880
So Istio is a new way of
managing microservices

00:42:37.880 --> 00:42:39.890
in a mesh.

00:42:39.890 --> 00:42:43.670
We have a ton of customers
that have built microservices

00:42:43.670 --> 00:42:44.810
on PCF.

00:42:44.810 --> 00:42:49.320
And actually, PCF, or
Pivotal, is a partner of ours.

00:42:49.320 --> 00:42:53.030
And we have built integrations
between our platforms

00:42:53.030 --> 00:42:54.650
to ensure that, as
you're building out

00:42:54.650 --> 00:42:59.610
microservices and
deploying them onto PCF,

00:42:59.610 --> 00:43:02.870
you can also leverage Apigee
to provision what we call

00:43:02.870 --> 00:43:07.970
a microgateway or even use their
full-blown edge proxy to secure

00:43:07.970 --> 00:43:10.400
those microservices itself.

00:43:10.400 --> 00:43:14.610
Check out our Documentation
page for more details.

00:43:14.610 --> 00:43:17.520
All right, so we do
have a question here.

00:43:17.520 --> 00:43:21.020
Do we have Qwiklabs to try
out some concepts and labs

00:43:21.020 --> 00:43:23.910
