00:43:36.830 --> 00:43:37.920
well.

00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:40.340
From there, you can actually
play with it for free.

00:43:40.340 --> 00:43:42.980
Can Apigee help in
versioning off the API?

00:43:42.980 --> 00:43:44.240
Absolutely.

00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:47.240
So there are different
ways of versioning APIs.

00:43:47.240 --> 00:43:49.950
The one that we see
most common is actually

00:43:49.950 --> 00:43:57.950
through putting the V1 or V2 in
the URL, or URI, I should say.

00:43:57.950 --> 00:43:59.405
And that gives you
the ability to,

00:43:59.405 --> 00:44:04.070
again, deploy multiple versions
of the same API as well.

00:44:04.070 --> 00:44:06.230
Internally, within
Apigee, you also

00:44:06.230 --> 00:44:08.010
have the ability to
leverage something

00:44:08.010 --> 00:44:10.580
called Revisions,
where we keep a copy

00:44:10.580 --> 00:44:13.850
of your previous
deployment of an API proxy,

00:44:13.850 --> 00:44:16.570
which gives you an ability
to then roll forward or roll

00:44:16.570 --> 00:44:19.510
backwards as you need.

